+# Pickup reminders
+
+For whoever changes how members are reminded of a pickup, or proposes moving the reminder from SMS to email. The day
+before a pickup slot, larder sends the member one message saying their pantry order is ready; it goes by SMS, not
+email. Written after [issue 52](../../notes/issue-52.md), the latest of several proposals to switch to email, each of
+which had to be answered from memory.
+
+## Why SMS
+
+SMS costs about 40 euros a month and email is free, so switching keeps being proposed. It was tried from April to
+June 2025:
+
+- The email provider reported that 34% of the reminder emails were never opened.
+- Missed pickups rose from 6% of pantry orders to 13%. Each missed pickup is a packed bag whose fresh food is thrown
+  away at closing time.
+- Many members share one phone within a family and rarely check email; an SMS on that phone is seen.
+
+Larder switched back to SMS on July 1, 2025, and missed pickups were back to 6% by August. The maintainers closed
+issue 52 keeping SMS. A new proposal to use email needs an answer to the unopened reminders and the food they cost,
+not only the saving.
+
+## How it works
+
+`remind` in `larder/reminders.py` builds the message and sends it to the member's phone. The channel is the `CHANNEL`
+constant in the same file; it is `"sms"`, and any other value sends the same message by email instead.
